  "live_records": {
    "q-41247": {
      "dom_id": "step-q41247",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Determine the domain of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}{log}_{7}⁡(2x-3)+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "The domain of $y={log}_{7}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\nx>0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $2x-3$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n2x-3>0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & >0 \\\\ 2x & >3 \\\\ x & >\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in (\\frac{3}{2},\\infty ).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
