    "q-81997": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81997",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7)=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7)} & ={e}^{0} \\\\ 2x+7 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =-6 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
