      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the maximum value of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x-4)+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of the function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nHorizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range of a logarithmic function.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ and the function has no maximum value.",
